From 27ee4748f5680333093504552b0d99fd5ed5d3ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncanmcqueen <206344294+duncanmcqueen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:16:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Haiku AWT and sound peer, and fixes for Kaffe on
 Haiku

- gnu.java.awt.peer.haiku: an AWT toolkit with native Haiku windows,
  menus, file panels, cursors and clipboard.
- gnu.javax.sound.sampled.haiku: a javax.sound mixer that plays
  through the Haiku media server.
- native/jni/haiku-peer: libhaikupeer (-lbe -ltracker -lmedia), with
  JNI headers in include/.
- configure: --enable-haiku-peer, on by default on Haiku. It makes
  HaikuToolkit the default toolkit and registers the Haiku mixer.
  Look for socket functions in libnetwork too. Remove the stray
  spaces after 'statvfs \', which made new autoconf skip mmap.
- lib/Makefile.am: copy the service files that configure makes, so
  out-of-tree builds get them.
- cpnet.c: use gethostbyname_r only when its declaration is known.
- OpenTypeFontPeer reads fonts-<os.name>.properties first; add
  fonts-haiku.properties.
- Frame.setState() set the opposite state.
- Thread: create the thread-local map on first use (Kaffe).
- ResolverCache: create the cache before the TTLs.
- VMNetworkInterface: define IFF_RUNNING if missing (Haiku).

Run autoreconf -fi after applying this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
